# R50's factory audio is stored in Git LFS, not in the repository itself.
# Git keeps a small pointer file per sample; the audio lives in the LFS store.
# The scope is deliberately narrow -- only the two R50 sample trees that ship
# with the plugin. Loose WAVs elsewhere stay ignored by .gitignore, and
# old_factory_samples is a local archive that is not tracked at all.
#
# Cloning this repository requires git-lfs. Without it these paths arrive as
# pointer text rather than audio, and R50's shipped-multisample tests fail on
# files that look present but are not readable as WAVs.
Products/R50/factory_samples/**/*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Products/R50/Samples/*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
